The existing research defines a compact optional loop unlocked by clearing A2-L1. Collect three journal fragments by contact, then reach the opened exit; the checkpoint is before the final exchange. Reward is a completion stamp or cosmetic acknowledgement with no stat increase. The3–5minute range is a pacing estimate, without a timer or forced wait. Enemy count, loop dimensions and exact collection order remain authored choices. Defeat-all is not an objective.

The player decision is which fragment to collect next and where to stand during a normal Scout warning so its locked ray leaves a useful return route. Combat taps retain primary/blast meaning; fragments and exits use contact. This reuses ordinary Scout targeting, with no B05 last-completed-world-landing bait mechanic, new attack, boss, Handler or Tender introduction. Broad continuous dry ground and a reachable ordinary-primary/no-ammo/no-pickup opportunity remain required for supported loadouts.

Reuse the parent heath/sand/scorch, cylinder/lid/pit-edge, pines/trunks, Ray Scout actor/visual/adapter and shared lane warnings. Only three journal fragment props and an exit marker are documented additions. Pit/cylinder mouths are scenic boundaries, without descent, climbing, swimming or narrow planks. The parent HeathKit.build hardcodes L1 arrangement; it is a source family rather than an already authored O1 topology. Recompose existing modules under O1 ownership without changing accepted L1 production. Prop source, native scale, pivot, collision/occlusion and available/active/spent states must be recorded when introduced.

